// Phantasm-shape BasicSummon (the `unseen_servant.ron` shape): a decorative,
// non-agentic prop, not a fighter. `alignment: Some(Passive)` (no will of its
// own), `with_agent: false` (no independent behaviour to run),
// `incorporeal: true` + `has_health: false` + `phantom_illusion: true`
// (vanishes on the first hit), matching a fragile nature spirit rather than a
// combatant. `duration` matches the spell's own `Concentration(60)`.
//
// KNOWN GAP, dropped rider: the sheet's "mends the wounds of allies who
// share its presence" is not expressed here. No primitive lets a summoned
// NPC apply a passive heal-on-proximity effect to nearby entities --
// `BasicAura`/`StaticAura` grant that kind of zone effect directly, but this
// spell's own sheet `variant` is `BasicSummon`, and no summoned-NPC-as-
// walking-aura mechanism exists in `SummonInfo::Npc`. Ships as a moving,
// harmless decorative spirit only; the healing rider is a Lane B follow-up
// (a `SummonInfo` variant or NPC-carried aura would be new engine work).
// `body: Object(Pebble)` reuses `unseen_servant.ron`'s own "small,
// unobtrusive placeholder" body rather than inventing a new asset.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 0.75,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 1,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 3.0),
        body: Object(Pebble),
        scale: None,
        has_health: false,
        use_npc_name: false,
        loadout_config: None,
        skillset_config: None,
        duration: Some((secs: 60, nanos: 0)),
        alignment: Some(Passive),
        with_agent: false,
        incorporeal: true,
        phantom_illusion: true,
        delete_after_expiry: true,
    ),
)
